{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/298687-what-was-your-first-campaign","id":298687,"title":"What Was Your First Campaign?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-31T22:27:21-07:00","id":298687,"title":"What Was Your First Campaign?","content":"What was your first ever time gming World of Darkness? First time playing it?<br /> I'm interested to see how people got introduced to it, and the memorable stories they may have...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T23:25:03-07:00","id":298699,"title":"","content":"Both were in 1996, when my friend who'd introduced me to RPGs two years earlier with WEG Star Wars, brought Vampire the Dark Ages to summer camp. First half the summer he ran a solo game for me, and we swapped for me first GMing every on the second half. I am getting close to my personal 20th Anniversary with the cWOD.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it was that interesting... the stories were... kinda silly and ridiculous. I think my first WOD PC gained 20 dots in Disciplines in under a week of real time (we were playing ~2 hrs a day during free time).<br /> <br /> But I did get hooked on the WOD that summer. Within a year I'd moved on to WtA and MtA as my main games, and I've been playing on and off every since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T00:13:33-07:00","id":298727,"title":"","content":"First time I played cwod we started as humans visiting the new orleans carnival. During a gig of my characters band we got snatched and became shovelheads. We learned only the basic rules of the sabbat before we had to organize &quot;beverages&quot; for a big blood feast. During the blood feast a war party was started against a setite. We participated got to his haven, battled with another pack on the way. One of us was sent to torpor by a sniper who aimed for his burning cigarette (the player chose the flaw addicted to smoking, thinking it wouldn't be that bad since vampires don't have to worry about their health).<br /> <br /> I got low on blood and drank dry our Lasombra (god I hated this Character so much ^^) and when my Character didn't rage any more he realised what he'd done to his teammate. He decided to clean up his mistake by destroying him, trying to drink ALL of his blood. I ended up diablerizing him and botched my willpower roll so this guy endet up with a new good lucking body with a band and fame-background attached to it.<br /> We endet that game there and startet our first game where we actually created vampire characters instead of mortals.<br /> <br /> It was a lot of fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T04:21:11-07:00","id":298829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/298687-what-was-your-first-campaign#post298687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was your first ever time gming World of Darkness? First time playing it?<br /> I'm interested to see how people got introduced to it, and the memorable stories they may have...</div> </div> </div> </div>1994 a friend of mine started telling me about this new edition of some metalhead meets mythology game called Werewolf the Apocalypse. He bought the core and some 1st edition books including Valkenberg Foundation. After playing a quick one shot as Evan Heals-the-Past, Albrecht, and Mari Cabrah we made new characters with my buddy double timing fairly well as storyteller and pack character. As much as I'd like to say I remember my first character I can't beyond remembering it was a Silent Strider Theurge because Spirits!/Egypt! It didn't last long though as my interests always lay more with Vampire and it wasn't long before a separate group of friends began a regular Vampire the Masquerade 2nd edition game series that evolved into the Memphis by Night LARP we all played in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T06:46:01-07:00","id":298903,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> in Gary and Chicago as the first edition adventures came out in 1991-92, with some friends in high school. Yeah, I'm old. (One of those friends has moved back recently and is in my <b>V20</b> game, after <b>Blood And Smoke</b> last year. We try not to terrify the players who were born after that first game with too many stories of our ancient past...)<br /> <br /> I still like the first/second edition rulebook's intro setting and story, in which the players' characters attend a party hosted by the Prince of Gary and interacted with the other vampires around, with no big action scenes it really set out what made <b>Vampire</b> different from other RPGs we'd played at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T17:37:39-07:00","id":299500,"title":"","content":"2004 Vampire/Werewolf mixed genre LARP. I had heard of the WoD and of LARPing through the RPG milieu and had always wanted to try. Some guys and gals in theater class had gotten into the local game and recruited me. My first character was was a voodoo-themed Tremere with multiple personalities, because why not? The game had a lot of character death/turnover, which while frustrating on the one hand also let me experiment with a lot of clans and archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T00:38:31-07:00","id":299794,"title":"","content":"I'm almost certain the first CWoD character I ever made was for <b>Mage:</b> <b>The Ascension</b>, but the game never got off the ground.<br /> <br /> My first real chronicle was a Sabbat game in 2008. We were random shovelheads, and the Chronicle ended up taking us from Philidelphia to Montreal to Mexico City, and we helped determine the fate of the Regency. My character was a Pander, childe of a Serpent of the Light. I hadn't <i>really </i>learned the game very well, so his stats were Jack of All Trades to the nth degree (I had two dots in just about every Ability by the end of it). My character was a bit boring, but I fell in love with <b>Vampire </b>after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T01:26:13-07:00","id":299816,"title":"","content":"I have no idea when it was, other than in the 90's, but my first character was a Gangrel loner type, imaginative of me wasn't it, in a friends Camarilla game, not that there were any alternatives back then. The plot involved Tremere and their experiments, gone awry naturally, and in the end we broke into a Tremere research facility, with our on Tremere ally, although the experiment itself managed to escape it was a fun chronicle non the less and left a soft spot in me for the Gangrel Clan.<br /> <br /> Not long after that I got vampire myself and ST'd a few stories but I did spread out my interest into other parts of WoD as well, with Wraith stealing my breath away still being my favorite RPG ever. Unfortunately the RPG circles around here were always rather slanted towards Vampire so that is what most games were about due to popular demand. Including a Vampire LARP I participated in here and for a brief time in the late 90's early 2k's even had my own Changeling LARP going on but it unfortunately withered away when I left for military service and the ST I left in charge was a bit over her head I guess as the game died soon after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T04:51:49-08:00","id":299917,"title":"","content":"1998, Your average W:tA game, played a Ragabash Glass Walker, GM tossed me the Fang dagger at beginning of the game, which I promptly used (with an exceptional dice roll) to decapitate the BBEG well before we apparently were supposed to kill him. Oopsies. Well laid plans of mice and men and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T08:41:43-08:00","id":300027,"title":"","content":"2010, I played in a VTM LARP at a convention. Played a Brujah pre-gen character who was basically a typical 50's greaser (think The Fonz) named Samson but with a troubled past. Actually was commended on how well I played the character's personality, especially since it was very off-the-cuff and I had no experience with CWOD at all (having only had familiarity with Requiem a few months earlier). It was a good game though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T21:58:01-08:00","id":301820,"title":"","content":"95 or maybe 96 - i played a Mage in a big crossover game. I don't remember too much about it, but I do remember that I didn't fully understand the rules and wasn't always sure what was going on in the story because our ST was spastic and jumped around an awful lot. I got hooked on vampire when I mistakenly bought the wrong book and ended up with a vampire rule book and not a Mage one. After reading through that I was decidedly a vampire player and completely against the idea of a crossover ever happening again so long as I ran a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/751-dicemauler","name":"dicemauler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T08:21:34-08:00","id":304616,"title":"","content":"According to some Google-fu, it had to be 1996 as I had to secure my own copy of 1st edition <b>Laws of the Night</b> to play the <b>Vampire the Masquerade</b> LARP and it had just been released.<br /> <br /> Threw together a Native American Gangrel that didn't even last thru the night before getting himself in so much trouble that he would have been executed if he didn't flee the city. A lot of that was due to not having read the rules before playing. Got my book, read the rules, came back with one of my all-time favorite characters that I've reused multiple times and kept going in that same LARP for a year. Alexi Shostakov, former solider/muscle/enforcer/general purpose person to hurt and kill someone for the KGB. Embraced shortly after the fall of the Berlin Wall into the Gangrel Clan.<br /> <br /> Shortly after the first couple of sessions of the Vampire LARP, someone else was starting up a <b>Werewolf the Apocalypse</b> table top. I created another favorite recurring character as a Gurhal (my buddy tried to talk me into a Child of Gaia, but since it was just him &amp; me and the ST, the whole &quot;other Breeds BAD!&quot; didn't come up as much).<br /> <br /> Then I found <b>Mage the Ascension</b> and shortly after that <b>Wraith the Oblivion</b>.......and I was beyond hooked!<br /> <br /> I've had the opportunity to play or run every major splat of the Classic WOD but <b>Mummy the Resurrection</b>, and that was mostly from lack of interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:27:21-08:00","id":304944,"title":"","content":"My First campaign was a VTM game played via the multiplayer of the PC game <b>Vampire the Masquerade Repetition</b> back in 2001 which is also how I got into role playing and latter on actual tabel top games. I typically played with this one group which I like to call the Court of Azrural as that who the ST and head vampire of the city was called. <br /> <br /> The main premise of the games was what if the Promethean managed to secure a city(in this case Prague) and rule out while keeping out invaders mainly the Tremere and the Capidotions. I participated in 3 of their games the last of which I can't really remember, each time as a different character because my role playing the same character was kind of schizophrenic back then. The first game had to do with us confronting a bunch of Tremere created constructs which had to do with the 4 elements that were led by Azural's brother who dubbed himself &quot;The Firemaster&quot;. The second game involved onthoer group of Tremere who had made a giant war ghoul.<br /> <br /> And in the sheer shot in the dark that any of the people I'm about to mention see this, I'd like to give a special shout out to Azrual, Toni, Karl, Raven, Arinna, Carry, Grrr, Jake, Luke and Josh for introducing me to the wonderful world of role playing games and putting up with my at the time annoying 13 year old ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:36:04-08:00","id":305160,"title":"","content":"it was bad xD i lacked a lot of info, so it was a bit of hit and miss...<br /> i remember a campaing of reckoning in which one of the players went to Hell to save his girlfriend...<br /> <br /> did i mentioned i lacked enough info to make a setting as beliaveable as possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:55:18-08:00","id":308953,"title":"","content":"I discovered vampire only in University in 2001 and played my first game in 2002. RPG aren't popular or known in my country unless they're played in a computer! My first character was a Malkavian, traveling to Constantinople in the year of our Lord 1230. It was an instant addiction, but like Crowley I felt it was bad lacking way too much info, even my second character failed big. Third time is the charm and I quite enjoyed my Assamite.<br /> <br /> Memories of him? One of the memorable moments was when I tried infiltrating a Capadocian's haven to, hmmm, release him from his curse and give rest to his soul and being an expert infiltrated with Dexterity 5 Stealth 5, I decided not to use Silence of Blood. Because the stairs were wooden the ST told me to roll diff 6 to muffle the sound and I did the impossible, I managed to BOTCH the damn roll with 10 dice! Some damn assassin :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T07:13:57-08:00","id":312243,"title":"","content":"When I first had my baby, my whole life halted. I loved him. That said, for that first month I couldn't string much together beyond that. I was always a mess, and struggled to keep us both clean and fed while both of us were tired and cranky (I would later learn he had an intolerance that caused him stomach pain and kept him awake).<br /> <br /> I got into LARP online in the third month, and really appreciated that I felt I was getting my social group back. Gaming brings you together fast, I think because you feel like these fellow nerds get you better than your family sometimes.<br /> <br /> The ST for the venue I was playing in (Changeling) was also the ST for Mage, and it overwhelmed this person so much that they weren't comfortable running plot for either. They left Changeling to focus on Mage, and I was told it was likely Changeling might close if they didn't get an ST. I would lose my friends- what else in common did I have with them outside of Changeling? We all came from different age groups, occupations and countries!<br /> <br /> NO<br /> <br /> I piped up that I could do it. Changeling became my pet. I read every paperback/hardback/PDF I could get. I read chat groups for inspiration, and read Mind's Eye house rules galore. We got big. More friends for me. Another ST was brought on to help me with our now-big venue. My baby got over his intolerance. I got my sleep back. I kept the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3920-sarah-rps","name":"Sarah RPs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T20:40:58-08:00","id":312727,"title":"","content":"My first game was back when V:tM first came out. About a week after. I played a Gangrel street kid. There was a Nosferatu Malkavian and a Ventrue. all I remember was that the Ventrue could only feed on delivery persons. The game was very basic, we were all new in town. I got bored with my character after a few sessions and started a new one. the second one was a Brujah. The game didn't go anywhere as I remember. My second game was much better. It lasted over 4 years. I was 30 when I first played. I still love the games and I am currently running a W:tA game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T08:40:55-08:00","id":312972,"title":"","content":"First game was in '91, when it came out; Gangrel named Maggie (I still have her around, though I haven't played her in more than a decade -- she has survived some pretty heavy shit). We were well-connected, though, via our gaming club, and had access to the game before it was officially published, pre-'91; we were also playtesters for the LARP, back in the day, w/Mike and Ian, for a year, before it was published in '93 (and, although we like the later mechanical improvements for the LARP rules, we all *SO* missed the more clan-specific powers that the 1st. Ed. MET had, where for example the Toreador had Heightened Senses, Aura Perception, Celerity, Awe and Curse of Sutek -- the last one we all *loved* because it felt *so right* that the Toreador -- along with Malkavians, who also had access to that power -- could use it to influence emotional states/mindsets/demeanors; it worked well compared to the Ventrue having a little different form of Dominate power vs. the Malkavians', or how Brujah Presence powers were a touch different from Toreadors', etc...). Sorry -- got lost on a tangent there for a second....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}